abstract: >
  WSF-Bench is a regime-aware benchmarking architecture for sustainable monitoring
  of wood-related production and trade systems. The v2.0 Python core provides
  curated benchmark data, reproducibility scripts, diagnostic outputs, supplementary
  tables, and high-resolution figure exports for leakage-safe model comparison,
  execution-validity logging, no-fallback sensitivity analysis, paired statistical
  validation, regime-robustness assessment, focused recurrent-challenger evaluation,
  and grouped LightGBM interpretability.
keywords:
  - "regime-aware benchmarking"
  - "sustainable monitoring"
  - "wood-related value chains"
  - "time-series forecasting"
  - "execution validity"
  - "regime robustness"
  - "LightGBM"
  - "recurrent challenger"
